"commons-desc-page"}, "GPSMapDatum": {"value": "WGS-84", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "In <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thun\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Thun\">Thun</a>, Switzerland, trolleybus 5 of the Thun–Beatenbucht trolleybus system (part of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verkehrsbetriebe_STI\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Verkehrsbetriebe STI\">Verkehrsbetriebe STI</a>) is northbound on Freienhofgasse, and coming off of the Sinnebrücke, in Thun. All nine trolleybuses of the Thun–Beatenbucht system were built in 1952 by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berna\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Berna\">Berna</a>, to a length of 11 metres (36 ft), and five had bodies made by Carrosserie Gangloff (of Bern) while the other four had identical bodies by Ramseier &amp; Jenzer (of Biel). No. 5 had a Gangloff body.  The trolleybus line opened for service in August 1952 and closed in March 1982.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "1976, between 26 August and 1 September", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "ETH-Bibliothek Zürich / Image Archive / SIK_01-007248 / CC BY-SA 4.0 / <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://doi.org/10.3932/ethz-a-000506443\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.3932/ethz-a-000506443\">http://doi.org/10.3932/ethz-a-000506443</a>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q61999546\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q61999546\"><span title=\"Swiss architect, author and photographer as well as historian of technology and economics (1950–2022)\">Hans-Peter Bärtschi</span></a></bdi>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "true", "source": "commo